--TEST--
`Core\Program::constructors<T, C>()` refuses a `C` that is not a `callable(...)` type returning `T`, and names each listed class whose constructor `C`'s parameters cannot call, for too few, too many, a wrong type and a private constructor, at the call (`rule:programs/constructors`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:programs/constructors`: each row's `make` is
// `fn(<C's parameters>): T => new Class(<the same arguments>)`, checked where
// the call is written. The accepted call is first, so a member that stopped
// answering a well-formed one fails here rather than as a missing refusal.
interface Plugin {
    public function name(): string;
}

class Clock implements Plugin {
    public function constructor(public int $hour, public string $zone = "UTC") {}
    public function name(): string { return "clock"; }
}

echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::constructors<Plugin, callable(int): Plugin>()), "\n";

// Bare `callable` names no parameters to check the constructors against.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::constructors<Plugin, callable>()), "\n";

// A `make` returns a new `Plugin`, and `string` does not accept one.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::constructors<Plugin, callable(int): string>()), "\n";

// Not a function type at all.
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::constructors<Plugin, int>()), "\n";

interface Job {
    public function run(): void;
}

// Needs two arguments, and the function type passes one.
class Mailer implements Job {
    public function constructor(public string $host, public int $port) {}
    public function run(): void {}
}

// Takes no arguments, and the function type passes one.
class Sweeper implements Job {
    public function run(): void {}
}

// Takes an `int`, and the function type passes a `string`.
class Timer implements Job {
    public function constructor(public int $seconds) {}
    public function run(): void {}
}

// The constructor is private, so `new Vault(...)` is not allowed here.
class Vault implements Job {
    private function constructor(public string $key) {}
    public function run(): void {}
}

echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Program::constructors<Job, callable(string): Job>()), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0838]: `Core\Program::constructors` needs a `callable(...)` type returning `Plugin`, and `callable` is not one
%A
error[E0838]: `Core\Program::constructors` needs a `callable(...)` type returning `Plugin`, and `callable(int): string` is not one
%A
error[E0838]: `Core\Program::constructors` needs a `callable(...)` type returning `Plugin`, and `int` is not one
%A
error[E0839]: `Mailer`'s constructor cannot be called with `callable(string): Job`'s parameters
%A
error[E0839]: `Sweeper`'s constructor cannot be called with `callable(string): Job`'s parameters
%A
error[E0839]: `Timer`'s constructor cannot be called with `callable(string): Job`'s parameters
%A
error[E0839]: `Vault`'s constructor cannot be called with `callable(string): Job`'s parameters
%A
